cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as follows."
title: "TinyGuard-AI: An ARM Cortex-M4-Based TinyML Predictive Maintenance and Intelligent Sensor Monitoring System"
abstract: >-
  TinyGuard-AI is a reproducible end-to-end pipeline that trains a small
  multilayer perceptron on vibration features, quantizes it to INT8, exports the
  parameters as C headers, and runs the model as bare-metal firmware on an ARM
  Cortex-M4. The integer inference engine is verified against the Python
  reference implementation with zero prediction divergence across all 3000
  windows, and the dataset and generated headers regenerate byte-for-byte from
  the committed sources. Scientific limitations are intrinsic to this release:
  the vibration dataset is synthetic, and ARM execution is QEMU emulation. No
  physical accelerometer, machine or microcontroller was measured, and no
  inference latency or energy figure is reported. The reported classification
  accuracy reflects the separability of the synthetic generator rather than
  demonstrated model capability, and simpler baselines reach the same score.
